---
description: Auth, tokens, secrets, and backend authorization
globs: backend/app/core/security.py,backend/app/modules/identity/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

Authentication identifies the caller. Authorization decides what that caller
may do. Backend checks are authoritative. Do not trust a role, permission,
or `organization_id` supplied only by the client. Derive tenant scope from
the authenticated session.

Keep auth dependencies at the route boundary. Put the check close enough to
the operation that another entry point cannot skip it.

Use the helpers in `app/core/security.py` for password hashing and JWT
issue/verify. Do not invent custom cryptography. Never put tokens or
passwords in URLs or query parameters.

Never log passwords, access tokens, refresh tokens, API keys, or sensitive
personal data. Do not return those values in API errors.
